`94.920289%` is the exact answer to “how much of the package remains
blob-backed,” but it is **not** a defensible estimate of proprietary Even
source. Opaque spans still mix identified upstream libraries, first-party Even
code/data, vendor ports, generated assets, and proprietary controller images.
The source manifest does not yet assign every opaque byte an origin category,
so a precise “original, non-upstream source” percentage would be false
precision. Path and string evidence indicates first-party Even code is the
largest Apollo-main remainder. Origin-aware byte accounting is a separate
required ledger improvement.

